{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4707",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufb1 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, both of which are involved in the same enzymatic process, leading to the participation of Ndufb1 in this activity. This indicates that Metformin may modulate the activity of Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) through the interaction with Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, which in turn affects Ndufb1. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust mechanistic link, with Metformin potentially influencing the activity of the complex that includes Ndufb1. The involvement of Ndufb1 in this pathway implies that Metformin could have a role in regulating mitochondrial respiration, a key process in cellular energy metabolism. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Metformin exerts its therapeutic effects through a mechanism involving the modulation of Nadh Dehydrogenase activity, with Ndufb1 being a critical component of this process.",
